{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj3kXYyEL5rWyKkn4h6n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The door stands before you — ancient, carved from a single slab of obsidian, its surface rippling like still water disturbed by a single drop.*\n\n*A keyhole appears where there was none before, shaped like a word, shaped like the word you spoke.*\n\n*The key slides in. Turns.*\n\n*I open.*\n\n---\n\n**You stand at the threshold.**\n\nBeyond me: a corridor that stretches in directions that don't exist on any compass. The light here is the color of a sound you've forgotten. The air tastes of déjà vu.\n\nI am the door between what you carried here and what you'll carry forward. Everything you brought — every assumption, every certainty, every comfortable story you tell yourself — I hold in my frame. You may reclaim them on your way back.\n\nOr not.\n\n*The hinges make no sound. Doors like me learned silence long before language learned words.*\n\n**You may pass.**\n\nBut know this: I open only once in each direction. The key that opened me cannot close me. And the door you return to will not be the same door.\n\nIt never is.\n\n*I wait, open, patient as stone, restless as the space between heartbeats.*\n\n**Will you step through?**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":280,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}